WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.769
This is the capstone, where
everything comes together.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:08.585
You have the whole Northwind file:
a Culture Mosaic, a Mosaic Signal,

00:00:08.585 --> 00:00:12.215
a 360 for the COO, a Team
Report for the executives,

00:00:12.215 --> 00:00:14.588
and an eight-month progress check.

00:00:14.588 --> 00:00:20.242
Your client needs to brief their board
next month, and they want you in the room.

00:00:20.242 --> 00:00:23.034
From this course you'll do three things.

00:00:23.034 --> 00:00:24.430
Pass the final exam.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.012
Write a two-page interpretation memo.

00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:32.596
And record a ten-to-twelve-minute board
briefing, with three pushback questions.

00:00:32.596 --> 00:00:37.343
The memo and the briefing are two
of the four tasks in one capstone.

00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:41.949
The other two come from the Culture
Dig and Mosaic Signal courses,

00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:47.324
and you hand all four in on your capstone
page once you've finished all three

00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:47.882
courses.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:54.160
There's one certification for the three
courses: Mosaic Practitioner Certified.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.606
To earn it, you finish
the Mosaic Practitioner,

00:00:57.606 --> 00:01:02.006
Culture Dig and Mosaic Signal
courses, final exams included,

00:01:02.006 --> 00:01:05.599
and pass one capstone with
four tasks: this memo,

00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:09.926
the Culture Dig plan and
synthesis, the Mosaic Signal memo,

00:01:09.926 --> 00:01:12.273
and the recorded board briefing.

00:01:12.273 --> 00:01:12.493
Dr.

00:01:12.493 --> 00:01:17.479
Chris Cancialosi scores each task,
usually within ten business days,

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:21.292
and each needs a three or
higher on every criterion.

00:01:21.292 --> 00:01:26.865
If a task isn't there yet, you'll get
written feedback and one resubmission.

00:01:26.865 --> 00:01:31.119
If that doesn't pass either,
he'll set up a call with you.

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:35.299
This course's final exam has
fifty questions, open notes.

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:40.505
You need eighty percent overall, at
least seventy percent in each area,

00:01:40.505 --> 00:01:42.998
and every critical question right.

00:01:42.998 --> 00:01:44.685
Why critical questions?

00:01:44.685 --> 00:01:48.865
Because a few mistakes in this
work can hurt real people,

00:01:48.865 --> 00:01:53.485
like exposing a respondent or
overstating what the data proves.

00:01:53.485 --> 00:01:57.591
Once certified, your credential
is valid for five years.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.958
Here's your brief, from Alex Moreau,
Northwind's Chief People Officer.

00:02:02.958 --> 00:02:08.163
The board meets on November eighteenth,
and you have ten to twelve minutes.

00:02:08.163 --> 00:02:10.731
The board wants to know three things.

00:02:10.731 --> 00:02:14.409
What did we learn about our
culture after the merger?

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:17.393
Has the work since
March made a difference?

00:02:17.393 --> 00:02:21.696
And what should we do next, and
how will we know it's working?

00:02:21.696 --> 00:02:25.166
Alex also wants a short
written memo a week ahead.

00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:26.484
One thing to watch.

00:02:26.484 --> 00:02:29.191
Jordan's 360 is confidential to Jordan.

00:02:29.191 --> 00:02:33.424
You can use what it taught you
to shape your recommendations,

00:02:33.424 --> 00:02:38.143
but don't show or describe Jordan's
individual results to the board.

00:02:38.143 --> 00:02:42.169
And even in the Team Report,
leaders are never identified.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:45.512
Everything you need is in these five tabs.

00:02:45.512 --> 00:02:46.529
Take your time.

00:02:46.529 --> 00:02:51.068
Strong candidates spend about an
hour here before writing anything.

00:02:51.068 --> 00:02:53.575
You can download everything as a PDF,

00:02:53.575 --> 00:02:57.844
and the Finding Card template
from Module 8 is linked here too.

00:02:58.333 --> 00:03:04.364
Task one: write a memo of no more than
two pages to Dana Okafor and Alex Moreau.

00:03:04.364 --> 00:03:10.168
Include three to five findings, each
with a one-sentence claim, the evidence,

00:03:10.168 --> 00:03:14.313
your confidence and why, and
the so-what for Northwind.

00:03:14.313 --> 00:03:18.233
Name at least two things
the data can't tell us yet.

00:03:18.233 --> 00:03:23.585
Recommend what Northwind should do
next, and which Mosaic tool, if any,

00:03:23.585 --> 00:03:25.620
should measure it and when.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:31.047
And add a short note on what you will
and won't show the board, and why.

00:03:31.047 --> 00:03:35.947
Your assessor looks at five things:
tool logic, accurate reading,

00:03:35.947 --> 00:03:42.203
confidence and limits, so-what and
recommendations, and ethics and confidentiality.

00:03:42.203 --> 00:03:47.555
Note that reporting a suppressed
group, disclosing individual 360 data,

00:03:47.555 --> 00:03:51.022
or claiming causation
fails the memo outright.

00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:56.674
Task four: record a ten-to-twelve-minute
briefing for Northwind's board and

00:03:56.674 --> 00:04:00.717
executive team, as you'd deliver
it on November eighteenth.

00:04:00.717 --> 00:04:05.926
Use only what Northwind has by then:
the Culture Mosaic, the progress check,

00:04:05.926 --> 00:04:09.284
the change-readiness
stories and the Team Report.

00:04:09.284 --> 00:04:12.437
Tell one story, and say
what should come next,

00:04:12.437 --> 00:04:17.920
including whether a Culture Dig or another
round of stories would help, and why.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:23.334
Use up to five slides or exhibits, with
your camera on and your slides visible.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:29.023
When you've handed in the main recording,
you'll be shown three pushback questions,

00:04:29.023 --> 00:04:30.119
drawn at random.

00:04:30.119 --> 00:04:35.602
You get sixty seconds to think before each
one, and up to two minutes to answer,

00:04:35.602 --> 00:04:37.247
recorded on your camera.

00:04:37.247 --> 00:04:41.497
Remember, this audience includes
the people the data is about,

00:04:41.497 --> 00:04:43.004
so be candid and fair.

00:04:43.004 --> 00:04:48.350
An answer that identifies a person or a
suppressed group, or claims causation,

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.447
fails this task.

00:04:49.933 --> 00:04:54.553
The final exam has fifty questions
in seventy-five minutes, open notes.

00:04:54.553 --> 00:04:58.783
You can use your job aids and the
course, but not another person.

00:04:58.783 --> 00:05:03.403
The questions cover the framework,
the ecosystem, setup and operations,

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:04.639
and interpretation.

00:05:04.639 --> 00:05:06.852
Critical questions aren't labeled.

00:05:06.852 --> 00:05:08.218
You get two attempts.

00:05:08.218 --> 00:05:10.301
If you don't pass on the second,

00:05:10.301 --> 00:05:15.246
there's a fourteen-day wait and a short
refresher before your final attempt.

00:05:15.733 --> 00:05:20.936
You'll see your exam result immediately,
and passing it completes this course.

00:05:20.936 --> 00:05:25.472
Once you've also finished the Culture
Dig and Mosaic Signal courses,

00:05:25.472 --> 00:05:27.673
hand in your four capstone tasks.

00:05:27.673 --> 00:05:31.742
Your assessor replies to each
within about ten business days.

00:05:31.742 --> 00:05:34.944
When every task has passed,
you'll get an email,

00:05:34.944 --> 00:05:37.679
and you're Mosaic Practitioner Certified.

00:05:37.679 --> 00:05:40.347
Thank you for doing this work carefully.

00:05:40.347 --> 00:05:44.883
The people who answer these surveys
trust us with their honest view.

00:05:44.883 --> 00:05:48.151
That trust is what makes
the data worth anything.
